================================================================================
SECTION F: KEY FINDINGS
================================================================================

1. MIGRATIONS 0001-0014: SANDBOX = CLOSEST MATCH (0d73697)
   The sandbox baseline migrations are byte-identical to the v5.1.0 merge state.
   All 13 differences vs origin HEAD were introduced by origin's post-merge ENUM
   fix commits. This confirms the sandbox was derived from the v5.1.0 state.

2. THE "HYBRID ENUM FIX" (0001-0013 differences)
   Two types of changes:
   a) ENUM creation: idempotent DO/EXCEPTION blocks → direct CREATE TYPE
   b) Column type: sa.Enum() → postgresql.ENUM(create_type=False)
   c) ONE REAL SCHEMA DIFF: prompt_id String(36) → UUID in storyboard_scenes
   
   On a CLEAN database (fresh install), both produce the same schema except
   for the prompt_id type difference. On an EXISTING database with ENUMs
   already created, the sandbox version (idempotent) is safer.

3. MIGRATION 0015: FUNCTIONALLY EQUIVALENT
   Both sandbox and origin add the same is_active Boolean column to users
   with the same type, nullable, and default. Only documentation differs.

4. MIGRATION 0016: REVISION CHAIN CONFLICT
   This is the critical reconciliation point:
   - Sandbox 0016 adds created_by to projects
   - Origin 0016 adds power_tdp_w to gpu_nodes
   - Both claim the same revision position
   - BOTH changes are needed for complete functionality
   - Reconciliation requires renumbering one chain

5. SANDBOX 0017-0022: ALL ADDITIVE, LOW CONFLICT RISK
   These are all simple column additions or index creation.
   None conflict with existing origin schema.
   All address genuine schema gaps or bug fixes.

6. ORIGIN HAS power_tdp_w; SANDBOX DOES NOT
   The sandbox is missing:
   - Migration 0016_add_power_tdp_w.py
   - ORM model column (gpu_node.py doesn't define power_tdp_w)
   This is a genuine feature gap in the sandbox.

================================================================================
SECTION G: RECONCILIATION REQUIREMENTS
================================================================================

For reconciliation, the following would need to be addressed:

REQUIREMENT 1: Decide which ENUM syntax to use
  Option A: Keep sandbox's idempotent DO/EXCEPTION approach (safer for re-runs)
  Option B: Adopt origin's direct CREATE TYPE + postgresql.ENUM (cleaner)
  Impact: 13 migration files

REQUIREMENT 2: Resolve prompt_id type (String(36) vs UUID)
  This is a REAL schema difference in storyboard_scenes.
  Must decide which type to use and ensure ORM model matches.

REQUIREMENT 3: Resolve migration 0016 chain conflict
  Option A: Keep sandbox 0016 (created_by), renumber origin's power_tdp_w
  Option B: Keep origin 0016 (power_tdp_w), renumber sandbox's created_by
  Option C: Merge into unified chain with new numbering
  Either way, BOTH columns need to end up in the final schema.

REQUIREMENT 4: Integrate sandbox 0017-0022 into origin chain
  These need to be renumbered to come after whatever 0016 resolution is chosen.
  All are additive and low-risk.

REQUIREMENT 5: Add power_tdp_w to sandbox ORM model
  If sandbox work continues, gpu_node.py needs the power_tdp_w column
  added to match the origin model and migration.

